From: QVAC SDK Pod <noreply@tether.io>
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-metal: handle NULL from ggml_metal_buffer_init

ggml_metal_buffer_init() can legitimately return NULL when the
underlying MTLDevice newBufferWithLength: fails (Metal heap exhaustion,
device lost, OS-level eviction on iOS warm relaunches with cached
models, etc.). The two callers in ggml-metal.cpp would then dereference
the NULL pointer one line later via ggml_metal_buffer_is_shared(res),
crashing with EXC_BAD_ACCESS / KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at offset 0x10
(struct ggml_metal_buffer's is_shared field).

Repro on iPhone 16 (iOS 18, ggml-speech @speech): warm-relaunch
QVACTestConsumer with the chatterbox TTS suite filtered in and cached
models on disk; bake_voice_conditioning() inside
tts_cpp::chatterbox::Engine::Impl::Impl() funnels through
ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors -> ..._alloc_buffer -> SIGSEGV.

Fix: return NULL from ..._alloc_buffer when ggml_metal_buffer_init
fails. This is the standard ggml-backend contract for allocation
failure; downstream callers (ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors etc.)
already propagate NULL up to the consumer, where chatterbox's
override-buffer path turns it into a clean
"Engine: alloc override buffer failed" std::runtime_error instead of
a hard crash.

Also add a defensive NULL guard inside ggml_metal_buffer_is_shared
itself so any other future caller cannot trigger the same SIGSEGV.

---
 src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m | 4 ++++
 src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp      | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m b/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
--- a/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
+++ b/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
@@ -1595,6 +1595,10 @@ void * ggml_metal_buffer_get_base(ggml_metal_buffer_t buf) {
 }
 
 bool ggml_metal_buffer_is_shared(ggml_metal_buffer_t buf) {
+    if (buf == NULL) {
+        // Defensive: callers may pass the result of a failed buffer init.
+        return false;
+    }
     return buf->is_shared;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp b/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp
--- a/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp
+++ b/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp
@@ -195,6 +195,10 @@ static ggml_backend_buffer_t ggml_backend_metal_buffer_type_alloc_buffer(ggml_ba
 static ggml_backend_buffer_t ggml_backend_metal_buffer_type_alloc_buffer(ggml_backend_buffer_type_t buft, size_t size, bool shared) {
     ggml_metal_device_t ctx_dev = (ggml_metal_device_t)buft->device->context;
     ggml_metal_buffer_t res = ggml_metal_buffer_init(ctx_dev, size, shared);
+    if (res == NULL) {
+        // Metal device allocation failed; surface as backend-alloc failure.
+        return NULL;
+    }
 
     ggml_backend_buffer_i buf_i = ggml_metal_buffer_is_shared(res)
         ? ggml_backend_metal_buffer_shared_i
